  "worked_solution": "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=-2+7=5.$",
